":54,"sd":null},{"k":"24:55","t":"Allāh has promised those who have believed among you and done righteous deeds that He will surely grant them succession [to authority] upon the earth just as He granted it to those before them and that He will surely establish for them [therein] their religion which He has preferred for them and that He will surely substitute for them, after their fear, security, [for] they worship Me, not associating anything with Me. But whoever disbelieves after that - then those are the defiantly disobedient.","j":18,"h":36,"s":24,"a":55,"sd":null},{"k":"24:56","t":"And establish prayer and give zakāh and obey the Messenger - that you may receive mercy.","j":18,"h":36,"s":24,"a":56,"sd":null},{"k":"24:57","t":"Never think that the disbelievers are causing failure [to Allāh] upon the earth. Their refuge will be the Fire - and how wretched the destination.","j":18,"h":36,"s":24,"a":57,"sd":null},{"k":"24:58","t":"O you who have believed, let those whom your right hands possess and those who have not [yet] reached puberty among you ask permission of you [before entering] at three times: before the dawn prayer and when you put aside your clothing [for rest] at noon and after the night prayer. [These are] three times of privacy for you. There is no blame upon you nor upon them beyond these [periods], for they continually circulate among you - some of you, among others. Thus does Allāh make clear to you the verses [i.e., His ordinances]; and Allāh is Knowing and Wise.","j":18,"h":36,"s":24,"a":58,"sd":null}],"juz":18,"hizb":36,"surahs":[24],"sajdah":false}